{"title":"Career roadmap · Merchandiser","role":"Merchandiser","summary":"A Merchandiser in the textile and apparel industry coordinates between buyers, design/product-development teams, production, sourcing, quality, suppliers and logistics to ensure products are developed and delivered according to specification, cost, quality and delivery timelines.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Textile Engineering / Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"B.Tech/B.E. Textile Engineering / Technology is strongly aligned because textile engineering provides technical knowledge of fibres, yarns, fabrics, processing, garment manufacturing, quality and production."},{"type":"note","label":"Career-route check","text":"Direct alignment. A practical route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech Textile","Merchandising/Product Development Intern","Merchandising Executive","Merchandiser","Senior Merchandiser","Merchandising Manager"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build textile technology, garment, costing, sourcing and communication skills; enter as Merchandising Executive"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in apparel, export, retail, technical textiles or product development"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress to Senior Merchandiser, Merchandising Manager or Product Development Manager"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead merchandising, sourcing, product development or global apparel/textile business"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Textile fundamentals"},{"text":"Fibres, yarns, fabrics"},{"text":"Textile identification portfolio"},